-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551144} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18700c44-863c-5283-8d80-b4ecba9f9a9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550422} {:answer/id #uuid "44d62fec-1344-5409-9e10-19b41bcbaf7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{nx}{\\pi })" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550529} {:answer/id #uuid "b4c2430c-0c6a-549e-aa2b-e39d8ffb22dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550860} {:answer/id #uuid "b70050b3-2831-538a-98f7-589a10e9520d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{nx}{\\pi })" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550868} {:answer/id #uuid "b732912b-9781-517d-a1b3-41138feb28b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{nx}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550870} {:answer/id #uuid "d386d763-aaac-543d-9911-63e1963b04ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{nx}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550941}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b4c2430c-0c6a-549e-aa2b-e39d8ffb22dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550860} :answer-field/id #uuid "b47fccdc-c568-5695-8718-41b3bbde7ccf" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551174}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ed658204-766e-56cd-a12e-1cf2b14b40f7" :question/math-academy-id "q-343391" :question/problem "Let $f(x)$ be the $2\\pi $-periodic extension of the function $F(x)=3{x}^{2}$ defined on $[-\\pi ,\\pi ).$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below, showing the derivation of a series converging to the $2\\pi $-periodic extension of \n\n$$\nG(x)={x}^{3}={\\int }_{0}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nfrom the corresponding Fourier series of $f(x).$\n\nThe Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\n3{x}^{2}∼{\\pi }^{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{12(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}}{{field-1}}.\n$$\n\nSince $f$ is \n{{field-2}} \non $R,$ we may integrate its Fourier series term-by-term to get\n\n$$\n{x}^{3}∼{\\pi }^{2}x+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{{field-3}}\\cdot {{field-4}}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that $F(x)$ is an even function. So, the Fourier series of its $2L$-periodic extension has the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{{a}_{0}}{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{n\\pi x}{L}).\n$$\n\nIn our case, $L=\\pi $ and we are already given the coefficients for $n\\ge 1.$ Thus, the Fourier series of $f(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)∼{\\pi }^{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{12(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nx).\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the function $F$ is continuous on $(-\\pi ,\\pi ).$ \nTherefore, the $2\\pi $-periodic extension $f$ is $\\text{piecewise continuous}$ on $R,$ so we may integrate its Fourier series term-by-term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{x}3{t}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t & ∼{\\int }_{0}^{x}({\\pi }^{2}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{12(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(nt))\\text{d}t \\\\ [{t}^{3}]_{0}^{x} & ∼[{\\pi }^{2}t]_{0}^{x}+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{12(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{2}}\\cdot [\\frac{1}{n}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(nt)]_{0}^{x} \\\\ {x}^{3} & ∼{\\pi }^{2}x+{\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\,\\frac{12(-1)^{n}}{{n}^{3}}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(nx)\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551353 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8063e78c-b15b-5158-9362-eae8ddeee9b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}-2\\sqrt{5}}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550693} {:answer/id #uuid "86c77418-8966-566d-a663-c864416cbf71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2+\\sqrt{15}}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550708} {:answer/id #uuid "dc24debd-ea85-5a42-99f4-725ec24bcaa3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2-\\sqrt{15}}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550966} {:answer/id #uuid "fb8359f2-1d22-508a-92f8-0e7f72b7d4ae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{5}}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551043} {:answer/id #uuid "fdcce495-5552-55ea-89df-1f5a9fdec70c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}+\\sqrt{3}}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551050}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dc24debd-ea85-5a42-99f4-725ec24bcaa3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2-\\sqrt{15}}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550966} :answer-field/id #uuid "45d5c494-ab4a-516a-a05d-cf2961b1ecb2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551108}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f8787df3-5e2e-5b10-9759-f8010831da06" :question/math-academy-id "q-144400" :question/problem "Suppose that for the angles $u$ and $v,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡v=\\frac{1}{2},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡v=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡u=-\\frac{2}{3}.\n$$\n\nGiven that $u$ lies in the third quadrant, find the value of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u-v).$" :question/worked-solution "First, recall the difference formula for sine:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u-v)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v-\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v\n$$\n\nWe know the values of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡v$, $\\operatorname{cos}⁡v$, and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡u.$ To find the missing value of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡u$, we can use the Pythagorean identity:\n\n$$\n{sin}^{2}⁡u+{cos}^{2}⁡u=1\\,⟹\\,{sin}^{2}⁡u=1-{cos}^{2}⁡u\n$$\n\nSubstituting our values into the Pythagorean identity, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{sin}^{2}⁡u & =1-{cos}^{2}⁡u \\\\  & =1-{(-\\frac{2}{3})}^{2} \\\\  & =1-{(\\frac{2}{3})}^{2} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{{2}^{2}}{{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =1-\\frac{4}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{9}-\\frac{4}{9} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡u & =\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{5}{9}} \\\\  & =\\pm \\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're given that $u$ lies in the third quadrant, where sine is negative. So, we disregard the positive value, and we have \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡u=-\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3}.\n$$\n\nWe can now apply the difference formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(u-v) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡u\\operatorname{cos}⁡v-\\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\operatorname{sin}⁡v \\\\  & =(-\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{3})(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})-(-\\frac{2}{3})(\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{15}}{6}+\\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2-\\sqrt{15}}{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551532 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "51b570f2-170f-50b9-b0a5-9563089e0914" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-12)\\,\\mathbf i+(-4)\\,\\mathbf j+(-18)\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551553} {:answer/id #uuid "85d95e24-11f1-5424-b411-e0cba95ba1d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- \\frac{3}{7})\\,\\mathbf i+(- \\frac{1}{7})\\,\\mathbf j+(- \\frac{3}{7})\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551566} {:answer/id #uuid "b6d64b4c-f8eb-5e52-a731-c64e6c9515d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{9}{49})\\,\\mathbf i+(\\frac{3}{49})\\,\\mathbf j+(\\frac{3}{49})\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551579} {:answer/id #uuid "b8cf17ec-9cf4-5d4b-ac5b-642ccc70904b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- \\frac{12}{49})\\,\\mathbf i+(- \\frac{4}{49})\\,\\mathbf j+(- \\frac{18}{49})\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551581} {:answer/id #uuid "eddd4ced-d849-5ca7-ab21-5aa50e4a8fb1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- \\frac{30}{49})\\,\\mathbf i+(- \\frac{10}{49})\\,\\mathbf j+(- \\frac{24}{49})\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551596}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b8cf17ec-9cf4-5d4b-ac5b-642ccc70904b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- \\frac{12}{49})\\,\\mathbf i+(- \\frac{4}{49})\\,\\mathbf j+(- \\frac{18}{49})\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551581} :answer-field/id #uuid "c14bbab2-5183-5313-8025-08879f6edb60" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551584}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "01b80278-13c1-5bc7-888c-457bedd82092" :question/problem "Evaluate $∇g(x,y,z)$ at the point $(1,3,1)$ if $g(x,y,z)=- \\frac{x y z}{3 x + y + z}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{x}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(- \\frac{x y z}{3 x + y + z}) \\\\  & =\\frac{(3 x + y + z)(- y z)-(- x y z)(3)}{(3 x + y + z)^2} \\\\  & =- \\frac{y z \\left(y + z\\right)}{\\left(3 x + y + z\\right)^{2}} \\\\ {g}_{y}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(- \\frac{x y z}{3 x + y + z}) \\\\  & =\\frac{(3 x + y + z)(- x z)-(- x y z)(1)}{(3 x + y + z)^2} \\\\  & =- \\frac{x z \\left(3 x + z\\right)}{\\left(3 x + y + z\\right)^{2}} \\\\ {g}_{z}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(- \\frac{x y z}{3 x + y + z}) \\\\  & =\\frac{(3 x + y + z)(- x y)-(- x y z)(1)}{(3 x + y + z)^2} \\\\  & =- \\frac{x y \\left(3 x + y\\right)}{\\left(3 x + y + z\\right)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇g(x,y,z) & ={g}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,\\mathbf i+{g}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,\\mathbf j+{g}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,\\mathbf k \\\\  & =(\\frac{3 x y z}{\\left(3 x + y + z\\right)^{2}} - \\frac{y z}{3 x + y + z})\\,\\mathbf i+(\\frac{x y z}{\\left(3 x + y + z\\right)^{2}} - \\frac{x z}{3 x + y + z})\\,\\mathbf j+(\\frac{x y z}{\\left(3 x + y + z\\right)^{2}} - \\frac{x y}{3 x + y + z})\\,\\mathbf k \\\\ ∇g(1,3,1) & =(\\frac{(7)(-3)-(-3)(3)}{(7)^2})\\,\\mathbf i+(\\frac{(7)(-1)-(-3)(1)}{(7)^2})\\,\\mathbf j+(\\frac{(7)(-3)-(-3)(1)}{(7)^2})\\,\\mathbf k \\\\  & =(- \\frac{12}{49})\\,\\mathbf i+(- \\frac{4}{49})\\,\\mathbf j+(- \\frac{18}{49})\\,\\mathbf k \\\\  & =(- \\frac{12}{49})\\,\\mathbf i+(- \\frac{4}{49})\\,\\mathbf j+(- \\frac{18}{49})\\,\\mathbf k\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551543 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "08f20dac-6288-5051-a0c9-656192ea317e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{54}{121})\\,\\mathbf i+(- \\frac{18}{121})\\,\\mathbf j+(\\frac{18}{121})\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551535} {:answer/id #uuid "1b82d1e6-c06d-5bc5-a3be-ca74e8368591" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- \\frac{6}{11})\\,\\mathbf i+(- \\frac{18}{11})\\,\\mathbf j+(- \\frac{6}{11})\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551539} {:answer/id #uuid "2beb0246-9a96-5b86-b925-3ee4afed1adc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-12)\\,\\mathbf i+(-216)\\,\\mathbf j+(-48)\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551541} {:answer/id #uuid "30d13711-2fa2-5805-aef5-71db8eb39744" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- \\frac{12}{121})\\,\\mathbf i+(- \\frac{216}{121})\\,\\mathbf j+(- \\frac{48}{121})\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551545} {:answer/id #uuid "e6e4497f-d6d4-5ce0-a5a1-5acd3a94ffb8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- \\frac{120}{121})\\,\\mathbf i+(- \\frac{180}{121})\\,\\mathbf j+(- \\frac{84}{121})\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551593}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "30d13711-2fa2-5805-aef5-71db8eb39744" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- \\frac{12}{121})\\,\\mathbf i+(- \\frac{216}{121})\\,\\mathbf j+(- \\frac{48}{121})\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551545} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf24e375-8a4c-5062-b9e8-dd5c1bf1791d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551583}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2d2b5e18-84ca-5425-a8f7-9933f3d81196" :question/problem "Evaluate $∇g(x,y,z)$ at the point $(3,1,3)$ if $g(x,y,z)=- \\frac{2 x y z}{3 x - y + z}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{g}_{x}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(- \\frac{2 x y z}{3 x - y + z}) \\\\  & =\\frac{(3 x - y + z)(- 2 y z)-(- 2 x y z)(3)}{(3 x - y + z)^2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2 y z \\left(y - z\\right)}{\\left(3 x - y + z\\right)^{2}} \\\\ {g}_{y}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(- \\frac{2 x y z}{3 x - y + z}) \\\\  & =\\frac{(3 x - y + z)(- 2 x z)-(- 2 x y z)(-1)}{(3 x - y + z)^2} \\\\  & =- \\frac{2 x z \\left(3 x + z\\right)}{\\left(3 x - y + z\\right)^{2}} \\\\ {g}_{z}(x,y,z) & =\\frac{∂}{∂z}(- \\frac{2 x y z}{3 x - y + z}) \\\\  & =\\frac{(3 x - y + z)(- 2 x y)-(- 2 x y z)(1)}{(3 x - y + z)^2} \\\\  & =- \\frac{2 x y \\left(3 x - y\\right)}{\\left(3 x - y + z\\right)^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the gradient is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇g(x,y,z) & ={g}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,\\mathbf i+{g}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,\\mathbf j+{g}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,\\mathbf k \\\\  & =(\\frac{6 x y z}{\\left(3 x - y + z\\right)^{2}} - \\frac{2 y z}{3 x - y + z})\\,\\mathbf i+(- \\frac{2 x y z}{\\left(3 x - y + z\\right)^{2}} - \\frac{2 x z}{3 x - y + z})\\,\\mathbf j+(\\frac{2 x y z}{\\left(3 x - y + z\\right)^{2}} - \\frac{2 x y}{3 x - y + z})\\,\\mathbf k \\\\ ∇g(3,1,3) & =(\\frac{(11)(-6)-(-18)(3)}{(11)^2})\\,\\mathbf i+(\\frac{(11)(-18)-(-18)(-1)}{(11)^2})\\,\\mathbf j+(\\frac{(11)(-6)-(-18)(1)}{(11)^2})\\,\\mathbf k \\\\  & =(- \\frac{12}{121})\\,\\mathbf i+(- \\frac{216}{121})\\,\\mathbf j+(- \\frac{48}{121})\\,\\mathbf k \\\\  & =(- \\frac{12}{121})\\,\\mathbf i+(- \\frac{216}{121})\\,\\mathbf j+(- \\frac{48}{121})\\,\\mathbf k\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551550 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "326a1a4f-342f-55b4-a110-a2709831b255" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{5}{8})\\,\\mathbf i+(\\frac{1}{16})\\,\\mathbf j+(- \\frac{11}{16})\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551546} {:answer/id #uuid "5e3bfb05-0026-500e-ab07-b20fa3d7a282" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\frac{7}{8})\\,\\mathbf i+(\\frac{7}{16})\\,\\mathbf j+(- \\frac{13}{16})\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551555} {:answer/id #uuid "7e3b866f-b033-5d4a-960c-12a16bdfb0e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(90)\\,\\mathbf i+(9)\\,\\mathbf j+(-99)\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186551562} {:answer/id #uuid "890840ec-d66a-5ea2-a525-97e6db70ac5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(- \\frac{1}{8})\\,\\mathbf i+(- \\frac{3}{16})\\,\\ma